CRUD OPERATIONS CODING QUESTION (Node.js + Express)
Problem Statement

Build a simple User Management REST API using Node.js and Express.js.

Do NOT use:

Database
Frontend
MongoDB/MySQL

Store data in an in-memory array.

Requirements
1. Create User
Endpoint
POST /users
Request Body
{
  "name": "Darshan",
  "email": "darshan@gmail.com"
}
Response
{
  "message": "User created"
}
2. Get All Users
Endpoint
GET /users
Response
[
  {
    "id": 1,
    "name": "Darshan",
    "email": "darshan@gmail.com"
  }
]
3. Get Single User by ID
Endpoint
GET /users/:id

Example:

/users/1
4. Update User
Endpoint
PATCH /users/:id
Request Body
{
  "name": "Updated Name"
}
5. Delete User
Endpoint
DELETE /users/:id